# Code owners for OneLiteFeatherNET/Falco.
#
# Two rules of this file are easy to get wrong, so they are spelled out here:
#
#  1. GitHub silently drops any owner that lacks write access to this
#     repository. A rule naming a team without access looks correct in review and
#     does nothing at all — no warning, no failed check. @OneLiteFeatherNET/falco-maintainers
#     holds admin here, which is what makes the rules below take effect.
#  2. Unlike .gitignore, the LAST matching rule wins. Order matters.
#
# The team follows the convention of the sister repositories, which own their code
# through a per-repository maintainers team: Cyano through cyano-maintainers, Aves
# through aves-maintainers. Membership is managed on the team, not in this file, so
# adding a maintainer never means editing CODEOWNERS.
#
# Verify after any change: `gh api repos/OneLiteFeatherNET/Falco/codeowners/errors`
# returns an empty list when every owner here is honoured.

# Default owners for everything, including the Java modules falco-anvil,
# falco-light, falco-instance and falco-benchmarks, and the documentation under
# docs/.
*                               @OneLiteFeatherNET/falco-maintainers

# Release, publishing and CI surface.
#
# These paths decide what leaves the repository rather than what it contains: the
# root build script holds the maven-publish setup, the repo.onelitefeather.dev
# endpoints and the single version line Release Please rewrites; settings.gradle.kts
# holds the credentialed resolution repository and the version catalogue; the
# wrapper is a binary executed by every CI run; and the workflows are thin callers
# of the shared OneLiteFeatherNET/workflows jobs that run with `secrets: inherit`.
# A mistake here ships a broken or mis-versioned artefact instead of failing a
# build, which is why they are pinned explicitly and not left to the default line
# alone. The owner is the same as above today; the point is that widening the
# default to a broader team later must not silently widen who can approve a
# release.
/build.gradle.kts               @OneLiteFeatherNET/falco-maintainers
/settings.gradle.kts            @OneLiteFeatherNET/falco-maintainers
/gradle/wrapper/                @OneLiteFeatherNET/falco-maintainers
/release-please-config.json     @OneLiteFeatherNET/falco-maintainers
/.release-please-manifest.json  @OneLiteFeatherNET/falco-maintainers
/CHANGELOG.md                   @OneLiteFeatherNET/falco-maintainers
/.github/                       @OneLiteFeatherNET/falco-maintainers
